/ref 17592186545356} {:answer/id #uuid "7184b1f4-449d-5810-934f-45a18f1048e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "weak positive linear correlation" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545414} {:answer/id #uuid "8231fe35-d847-50c6-b767-316e740854a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "strong positive linear correlation" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545442} {:answer/id #uuid "da723436-8cde-5bcc-ab9f-5d1691728692" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no linear correlation" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545603}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "548cb0fc-8599-5d8e-a01c-66d33541fbb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "strong negative linear correlation" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545356} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2702c34-c7e9-5325-9741-8ce3622c97cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545767}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e2c56edd-8fb8-5a8e-abe8-142f14623ed7" :question/math-academy-id "q-134103" :question/problem "![](images/04/04fbb73cfa465f4cb052f3347a8651bae48140441c4fbfa753d2bd86ac41dfe8.png)\n\nA group of students is interviewed. The scatter plot above shows the correspondence between the hours they spent playing video games daily the week before the literature exam and the grade they got on the exam. Which of the following best describes the correlation between the variables in the scatter plot?" :question/worked-solution "![](images/91/91d928d021c8715a24fdb7dc262bec53c30626d8649a2ac451c94f9c0ecc0db0.png)\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The points in the scatter plot seem to follow a straight line with a *negative* slope. So, we have a *negative* correlation.\n\n- The points lie pretty close to the corresponding trend line. So, we have a *strong* correlation.\n\nTherefore, the variables have a *strong negative* linear correlation."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545862 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083339 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebbc6b77-cd04-5509-b344-66feddfed1bb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Scatter Plot Given a Correlation Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cc1444b-fd8c-5102-acf6-a80893a9655f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ec/ec4b106cf763a4c54ee2b1d8eecf6e7b91e371b0dd38198502bd433ef7e6e371.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545255} {:answer/id #uuid "26ccb841-9c61-58c1-b74a-7d6ba6da7857" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a8/a866fcee0e975c0741299a5e1504470dbae44e18b541149c7d5e1e2acb9b32bd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545284} {:answer/id #uuid "8a10c856-18f3-5372-ad82-c037bac0b67c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/14/14258fd15361beae5d6e0655e81051b2e4bfd95d20b05dc98113558e43412f41.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545455} {:answer/id #uuid "9f1744c8-9253-57a1-9385-88741010bd5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ec/ec7a1b76ebbcc4965824be26bc4b1e630167b032855498df6d492a61461fecf9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545493} {:answer/id #uuid "be854c2e-00b5-5189-95d0-d391ce579514" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/10/10408bda83013b4decbf51370d20018004a1086a538322abbd0b9da1b910e4f2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f1744c8-9253-57a1-9385-88741010bd5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ec/ec7a1b76ebbcc4965824be26bc4b1e630167b032855498df6d492a61461fecf9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545493} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f1ba1af-342f-5fed-bb12-14097b1af01f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545691}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d339220f-f17c-55cf-8865-ba521fdebae7" :question/math-academy-id "q-134112" :question/problem "It's known that there is a linear correlation between the height (in $\\text{cm}$) and weight (in $\\text{kg}$) of a group of students in a particular class. Given that the correlation coefficient is $\\rho ≈0.45,$ which of the following scatter plots corresponds to this situation?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the linear correlation coefficient $\\rho $ satisfies the inequality\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\rho \\le 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\rho =1$ indicates a perfect positive correlation, and $\\rho =-1$ indicates a perfect negative correlation.\n\nTherefore, since $\\rho ≈0.45,$ there is a *weak positive* linear correlation in the data.\n\n- The *positive* linear correlation means that the data points should be scattered along a line with a *positive* slope.\n\n- Since the correlation is *weak*, most of the points should be scattered *far* from the trend line.\n\nTherefore, this situation corresponds to the following scatter plot.\n\n![](images/31/31aef47ad76d8cd4c7e967ccc7b8ca523eb3a20af440454bc7908bbe9441c918.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545868 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083338 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b973aca4-f9fc-5b5c-ab75-2329204993ce" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Correlation Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2042dc18-49bf-58fb-8c04-7b065a71ba6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\rho ≈0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545263} {:answer/id #uuid "a0758947-9149-585c-80e7-966a2a53f237" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\rho ≈0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545495} {:answer/id #uuid "e71cb635-681e-51e0-8351-d1cc6f433ab1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\rho ≈0.85" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545629} {:answer/id #uuid "edd640cf-5862-5d11-9954-da14ddb5d70f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\rho ≈-0.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545641} {:answer/id #uuid "ffb7ea0c-c555-50e6-b6f4-54644915ff89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\rho ≈-0.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e71cb635-681e-51e0-8351-d1cc6f433ab1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\rho ≈0.85" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545629} :answer-field/id #uuid "724bde99-b3bb-58df-81bd-552e8017bb6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545721}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e6c59cf1-e1f3-5c09-adfe-bd7d9e53be52" :question/math-academy-id "q-134120" :question/problem "![](images/9d/9dd43d8833be95bd8b13a98b65dddd1272501599b107053296302cb7fae7e58b.png)\n\nWhich of the following is the best approximation of the correlation coefficient for the data in the scatter plot above?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the linear correlation coefficient $\\rho $ satisfies the inequality\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\rho \\le 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\rho =1$ indicates a perfect positive correlation, and $\\rho =-1$ indicates a perfect negative correlation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n![](images/ae/aecc569c03ed874748993b77ed09a8a318dae23bcaea09334d98af9da36d8a87.png)\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The points in the scatter plot seem to follow a straight line with a *positive* slope. So, the correlation coefficient must be *positive*. Thus, we disregard the following values:\n\n$$\n\\rho ≈-0.75,\\,\\rho ≈-0.3,\\,\\rho ≈0\n$$\n\n- The points lie pretty close to the corresponding trend line. So, the correlation coefficient must be closer to $1.$ Thus, we disregard the following value:\n\n$$\n\\rho ≈0.25\n$$\n\nTherefore, the best approximation of the correlation coefficient must be $\\rho ≈0.85.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545798 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083338 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b973aca4-f9fc-5b5c-ab75-2329204993ce" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Correlation Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01a7c6d4-0487-53da-a22e-734216f21437" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\rho ≈0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545202} {:answer/id #uuid "7ef364a3-b3b6-5068-ab53-fbf996e0a6aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\rho ≈-0.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545433} {:answer/id #uuid "9c99d273-eee7-551e-991e-7d2f5b565510" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\rho ≈0.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545487} {:answer/id #uuid "ad977d26-9351-54cd-9449-7de02c055b6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\rho ≈-0.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545517} {:answer/id #uuid "e97f983b-8d60-5aec-9580-1d14d322c307" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\rho ≈0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e97f983b-8d60-5aec-9580-1d14d322c307" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\rho ≈0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545632} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fae3beb-3510-5939-afed-b54d6ee4d3a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545704}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "09efb2e6-1e80-53f4-bf82-55db52baf7d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-134122" :question/problem "![](images/f2/f2f569fe07310e8bd068cda0152b296d7b1189efec03720a0d3a043a7ab52d21.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows the relationship between the age of some people and the average number of cups of coffee they consume daily. \nWhich of the following is the best approximation of the correlation coefficient?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the linear correlation coefficient $\\rho $ satisfies the inequality\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\rho \\le 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\rho =1$ indicates a perfect positive correlation, and $\\rho =-1$ indicates a perfect negative correlation.\n\nFrom the plot, it seems that the data points are scattered randomly. Therefore, there is no linear correlation.\n\nTherefore, the best approximation of the correlation coefficient must be $\\rho ≈0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545841 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083338 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b973aca4-f9fc-5b5c-ab75-2329204993ce" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Correlation Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18de5bcf-ee53-583d-9955-d6382d059b1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\rho ≈0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545248} {:answer/id #uuid "4dde781b-7d3c-5e90-88e4-b6e543af6cd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\rho ≈-0.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545345} {:answer/id #uuid "52f0bd21-8e5a-5e90-94c5-b78bb36bcb81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\rho ≈0.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545352} {:answer/id #uuid "f4ea6508-51c1-5ee1-974c-71ab52286e70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\rho ≈0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545650} {:answer/id #uuid "fa53955d-d092-59ca-bedb-4ee2c6e6f178" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\rho ≈-0.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa53955d-d092-59ca-bedb-4ee2c6e6f178" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\rho ≈-0.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545662} :answer-field/id #uuid "f26454ee-b84b-57c9-bd6b-8ffaabec57a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545787}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9f7eb28b-e6d3-58a7-ad9a-3a6681ca1ee4" :question/math-academy-id "q-134125" :question/problem "![](images/4c/4c03191b325ee430f02216f35998db128ea99c6096222d489fa817f680e98d10.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows the relationship between the time some college students spend studying at night for their final exams and the number of hours they sleep per night. Which of the following is the best approximation of the correlation coefficient?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the linear correlation coefficient $\\rho $ satisfies the inequality\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\rho \\le 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\rho =1$ indicates a perfect positive correlation, and $\\rho =-1$ indicates a perfect negative correlation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n![](images/74/74aa691e42eea766595eede7d42d59e164509d6dbf3c8a609dd42e1196d11512.png)\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The points in the scatter plot seem to follow a straight line with a *negative* slope. So, the correlation coefficient must be *negative*. Thus, we disregard the following values:\n\n$$\n\\rho ≈0.8,\\,\\rho ≈0.4,\\,\\rho ≈0\n$$\n\n- The points are scattered quite far from the corresponding trend line. So, the correlation coefficient must be closer to $0.$ Thus, we disregard the following value:\n\n$$\n\\rho ≈-0.9\n$$\n\nTherefore, the best approximation of the correlation coefficient must be $\\rho ≈-0.3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545811 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083338 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b973aca4-f9fc-5b5c-ab75-2329204993ce" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Correlation Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fb66c80-1747-5cd6-b473-d39c5d64cf56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\rho ≈0.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545381} {:answer/id #uuid "647e1d76-8699-5f00-b950-f65a5d9a1e25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\rho ≈0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545390} {:answer/id #uuid "975ac0a8-2d8e-501d-aae1-278a3552d5f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\rho ≈0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545471} {:answer/id #uuid "b3b980a5-1b07-53a0-bd99-f5969d3971f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\rho ≈-0.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545526} {:answer/id #uuid "e340584d-ae6e-5e84-a152-3f6a2121b262" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\rho ≈-0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "975ac0a8-2d8e-501d-aae1-278a3552d5f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\rho ≈0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545471} :answer-field/id #uuid "157cc70f-8bfd-56d9-b601-f1ea6f2f9206" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545681}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2e20c6e9-8a1f-5520-84a5-13e0b1715760" :question/math-academy-id "q-134126" :question/problem "![](images/27/271e5f80ff6ab311bcdbc6b2725516b16a5c3fee63b6d219a59801c78d4f77e4.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows the relationship between the number of shirts and the number of pants sold in a store over a certain number of days. \nWhich of the following is the best approximation of the correlation coefficient?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the linear correlation coefficient $\\rho $ satisfies the inequality\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\rho \\le 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\rho =1$ indicates a perfect positive correlation, and $\\rho =-1$ indicates a perfect negative correlation.\n\nFrom the plot, it seems that the data points are scattered randomly. Therefore, there is no linear correlation.\n\nTherefore, the best approximation of the correlation coefficient must be $\\rho ≈0.$"}]}
